WEBVTT

00:00.519 --> 00:03.646
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.746 --> 00:06.847
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:06.882 --> 00:10.284
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.319 --> 00:13.554
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.589 --> 00:16.957
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:16.993 --> 00:20.294
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.329 --> 00:21.862
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:21.897 --> 00:23.797
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.833 --> 00:24.373
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.376 --> 00:38.312
We now return
to the NBA on TNT... on LSD.

00:40.016 --> 00:42.916
Man, I'm out my mind!

00:42.952 --> 00:46.754
Okay, my mom will be here
any minute for our spa day.

00:46.789 --> 00:48.756
"Spa," S-P-A.

00:48.791 --> 00:51.225
Yes, very good, Peter.

00:51.260 --> 00:53.627
And remember, while we're
off getting our massages,

00:53.663 --> 00:55.629
you and Daddy are gonna
spend the day together here.

00:55.665 --> 00:57.631
Aw, I don't want
to hang out with him.

00:57.667 --> 00:59.466
He's, like, not
ticklish anywhere.

00:59.502 --> 01:01.468
Look, I'm sorry,
but my mom said

01:01.504 --> 01:03.303
he can't be left alone
at home anymore.

01:03.339 --> 01:07.041
Last time, he went crazy and
moved all the furniture around.

01:07.076 --> 01:09.410
♪ Dancing, walking ♪

01:09.445 --> 01:12.413
♪ Rearranging furniture ♪

01:12.448 --> 01:15.249
♪ Babs is shopping ♪

01:15.284 --> 01:17.818
♪ I let the bird
out of the cage... ♪

01:20.289 --> 01:21.655
Hello, dear.

01:21.691 --> 01:23.657
Oh, I always forget

01:23.693 --> 01:26.160
you walk right into
the living room in your house.

01:26.195 --> 01:27.594
Hey, do you have
a Band-Aid?

01:27.630 --> 01:29.430
Nothing happened,
but I'm bleeding.

01:29.465 --> 01:31.625
You know what, I'll just
rummage through your bathroom.

01:33.035 --> 01:34.835
Man, spending
a whole day with him

01:34.870 --> 01:37.037
is gonna be worse
than eating at a ball park.

01:37.073 --> 01:38.872
Uh, I'll take
one terrible beer,

01:38.908 --> 01:40.874
filled up way too high,
so I spill most of it,

01:40.910 --> 01:43.711
and a too-long hot dog
on a too-short bun.

01:43.746 --> 01:45.145
And do you have
mustard and relish?

01:45.181 --> 01:46.780
Yeah, it's right there
between the entrance

01:46.816 --> 01:48.182
and the exit to
the bathroom.

01:48.217 --> 01:50.184
Perfect. And can I get
a bag of unsalted peanuts?

01:50.219 --> 01:51.618
You know, something
I would never eat

01:51.654 --> 01:53.020
anywhere else in the world?

01:53.055 --> 01:54.021
Sure, here you go.

01:54.056 --> 01:55.656
Great, great.

01:55.691 --> 01:58.292
I can't wait to have diarrhea
in the stall with no door

01:58.327 --> 02:00.661
while 20 guys wait
for me to finish.

02:04.433 --> 02:06.800
No.
Ah, no.

02:06.836 --> 02:08.802
All right,
left cankle, red.

02:10.840 --> 02:12.639
Right muffin top, blue.

02:16.078 --> 02:17.478
Sorry.

02:17.513 --> 02:19.713
Ugh, God, kill me.

02:19.749 --> 02:22.549
Stewie, I can't take any more
of Meg and her gross friends.

02:22.585 --> 02:23.984
Ah, ah,
hang on, hang on.

02:24.019 --> 02:25.853
I'm just finishing up
an e-mail to Delta.

02:25.888 --> 02:28.689
"I have never not screamed
at the top of my lungs

02:28.724 --> 02:32.092
during air pressure changes, and
I do not intend to stop now."

02:32.128 --> 02:33.093
Okay, what was it?

02:33.129 --> 02:34.728
Meg's friends.

02:34.764 --> 02:36.563
They're just so loud
and boring and annoying.

02:36.599 --> 02:39.399
Well, not everybody can be
as fascinating as you, Brian.

02:39.435 --> 02:40.834
Thanks for coming by.

02:40.870 --> 02:42.836
Hey, Brian, Mom
took the car.

02:42.872 --> 02:45.239
Can you give me and my friends
a ride to field hockey practice?

02:45.274 --> 02:49.243
Uh, I'm kind of helping Stewie
with an e-mail to Delta.

02:49.278 --> 02:50.744
Please, Brian.

02:50.780 --> 02:52.746
It would get them
out of the house.

02:52.782 --> 02:54.748
Well, that's true.
And I gotta do something,

02:54.784 --> 02:57.184
'cause they're more annoying
than ants at a picnic.

02:58.621 --> 03:00.053
Would you mind
turning that down?

03:02.892 --> 03:05.259
And you're not supposed
to be grilling.

03:05.294 --> 03:07.995
I know you can
understand me.

03:12.902 --> 03:16.470
So... what, uh, what
do you want to do?

03:16.505 --> 03:17.905
I don't know.

03:17.940 --> 03:19.306
Sucks that we're
stuck here alone.

03:19.341 --> 03:21.742
Wait a minute,
here alone.

03:21.777 --> 03:23.610
You thinking what
I'm thinking?

03:23.646 --> 03:25.445
This was not
what I was thinking.

03:25.481 --> 03:27.314
That's weird, it's not
what I was thinking either.

03:27.349 --> 03:28.916
I don't even know
how it happened.

03:28.951 --> 03:30.918
No, me neither, but this
spaghetti's not half bad.

03:30.953 --> 03:32.953
A "happy mistake,"
we'll call it.

03:36.425 --> 03:37.958
Now what do you
want to do?

03:37.993 --> 03:39.226
Well, we could
watch porn.

03:39.261 --> 03:40.627
Have you heard
of porn?

03:40.663 --> 03:42.062
Is that something
you're aware of?

03:42.097 --> 03:43.997
You have postcards
from France?!

03:44.033 --> 03:45.632
No, no, no, like...
like, on the computer.

03:45.668 --> 03:47.434
There's like tons
and tons of videos

03:47.469 --> 03:48.836
of people doing
it on there.

03:48.871 --> 03:50.270
Wait, l-let me understand:

03:50.306 --> 03:52.673
<i>You want to watch
that with me?</i>

03:52.708 --> 03:54.508
Well, not anymore,
you just made it weird.

03:54.543 --> 03:56.076
But there's other
stuff on there.

03:56.111 --> 03:58.345
You want to see a guy in
a human-sized hamster ball

03:58.380 --> 03:59.346
roll off a mountain?

03:59.381 --> 04:00.814
Uh, yeah.

04:02.818 --> 04:04.618
So this is in Russia?

04:04.653 --> 04:06.453
Somebody's gonna
slow him down, right?

04:06.488 --> 04:07.855
Whoa!

04:07.890 --> 04:09.690
I got
to e-mail that to Babs.

04:09.725 --> 04:10.924
She hates people.

04:10.960 --> 04:12.926
Huh, got a new e-mail here.

04:12.962 --> 04:14.928
And it's from a Nigerian prince.

04:14.964 --> 04:17.764
It says he's got millions
frozen in an account.

04:17.800 --> 04:20.767
All he needs is a hundred grand
to pay legal fees,

04:20.803 --> 04:23.670
and then as soon as he gets his
money, I get a million bucks.

04:23.706 --> 04:25.672
Wow, and he must
need it quick,

04:25.708 --> 04:27.674
'cause there was, like, a
bazillion typos in that e-mail.

04:27.710 --> 04:29.109
You got to send
that money.

04:29.144 --> 04:30.944
You think so?
Absolutely.

04:30.980 --> 04:33.347
I mean, can you imagine if
you make a million bucks?

04:33.382 --> 04:35.682
You'll be happier than the
guy on his wedding day.

04:35.718 --> 04:37.117
Thanks, everyone.

04:37.152 --> 04:38.518
Good-bye, Mom. Good-bye, Dad.

04:38.554 --> 04:40.354
Good-bye, friends.
Good-bye, free time.

04:40.389 --> 04:43.190
Farewell, sex.
So long, golf on TV.

04:43.225 --> 04:45.025
I'll miss you, privacy.

04:45.060 --> 04:47.461
Good-bye, being honest
about how many beers I've had.

04:47.496 --> 04:49.296
Nice knowing you,
my own choices.

04:49.331 --> 04:50.731
See ya later, money!

04:55.738 --> 04:56.904
Thanks for
the ride, Brian.

04:56.939 --> 04:58.338
Yeah, and thanks
for the lecture

04:58.374 --> 05:00.374
on what real music is,
Mr. Griffin.

05:02.878 --> 05:04.845
Geez, how many Snickers
could they eat

05:04.880 --> 05:06.680
in a five-minute car ride?

05:06.715 --> 05:09.383
Ah, crap, somebody left
their gym bag.

05:11.854 --> 05:14.655
God, it would've been real
easy to bring a gun in here.

05:14.690 --> 05:16.957
Where the hell'd they go?

05:20.195 --> 05:21.195
Oh, whoops.

05:27.603 --> 05:29.202
Wow.

05:32.775 --> 05:34.174
Holy crap.

05:34.209 --> 05:35.575
That was Patty.

05:35.611 --> 05:37.344
And she's got
a smokin' hot body.

05:37.379 --> 05:39.413
This is a bigger surprise
than when I found out

05:39.448 --> 05:41.281
Joe was a clown.

05:43.252 --> 05:45.252
I think
that belongs to me.

05:46.655 --> 05:48.622
I'm sorry you had
to find out this way.

05:48.657 --> 05:50.057
Okay.

05:50.092 --> 05:51.892
You won't tell
anyone, will you?

05:51.927 --> 05:52.893
No.

05:52.928 --> 05:55.295
You can tell people.

06:00.069 --> 06:01.735
Hey, so how
was the spa?

06:01.770 --> 06:04.137
Oh, it was fine, though
I don't know why they made us

06:04.173 --> 06:06.573
face each other during
the mother-daughter bikini wax.

06:06.608 --> 06:08.976
Did you two have
a nice afternoon?

06:09.011 --> 06:10.978
Sure did.
I made a million dollars!

06:11.013 --> 06:12.779
What?! How?

06:12.815 --> 06:15.248
Carter sent $100,000
to a Nigerian prince

06:15.284 --> 06:16.950
who's gonna give
him a million.

06:16.986 --> 06:20.053
Oh, Peter, don't tell me
you two fell for that scam.

06:20.089 --> 06:21.455
What? What are you
talking about?

06:21.490 --> 06:23.890
It's the oldest
e-mail scam out there.

06:23.926 --> 06:26.293
Their assets are frozen,
you cover legal fees.

06:26.328 --> 06:28.128
Blah, blah, blah.

06:28.163 --> 06:30.130
Oh, my God, he did say,
"Blah, blah, blah."

06:30.165 --> 06:32.065
You're never getting
that money back.

06:32.101 --> 06:34.468
What?! So that-that money's
just been Josh Hartnett-ed?!

06:34.503 --> 06:35.469
What's that?

06:35.504 --> 06:36.770
Gone! Disappeared!

06:36.805 --> 06:38.071
Never to be
heard from again!

06:38.107 --> 06:40.073
Isn't he in that
Showtime thing

06:40.109 --> 06:41.441
with the blood
and the hats?

06:41.477 --> 06:42.843
Look, the point is
I was swindled.

06:42.878 --> 06:44.277
I guess so.

06:44.313 --> 06:46.279
Well, come on, Mom,
the man was very specific

06:46.315 --> 06:48.315
that we need to go
put lotion on each other.

06:50.319 --> 06:52.119
Geez, I'm really
sorry, Carter.

06:52.154 --> 06:53.587
But at least you
have your health.

06:55.391 --> 06:56.757
Oh...

06:56.792 --> 06:57.958
You know,
this is your fault.

06:57.993 --> 06:59.393
You're the one
who said I should do it!

06:59.428 --> 07:01.261
Mm-hmm, there's
that judgy-ness

07:01.296 --> 07:03.196
Babs is always calling
me and talking about.

07:03.232 --> 07:05.599
Look, nobody steals
from Carter Pewterschmidt.

07:05.634 --> 07:07.667
I am going to Africa
and getting my money back.

07:07.703 --> 07:09.102
And you're coming with me.

07:09.138 --> 07:11.505
Africa?
We're going to Africa?!

07:11.540 --> 07:13.473
I wonder if it
will change us.

07:13.509 --> 07:15.609
But, of course,
it did change us.

07:15.644 --> 07:19.012
I've been working here for 50
years, pretending I'm a woman.

07:19.048 --> 07:20.814
: Do you ever
regret not having children,

07:20.849 --> 07:22.449
Mother Bernadette?

07:22.484 --> 07:24.785
Oh, I've had many children.

07:24.820 --> 07:27.821
♪ ♪

07:36.569 --> 07:38.135
We now return

07:38.171 --> 07:40.371
<i>to Kevin James Got Too Fat
To Be In Movies.</i>

07:40.406 --> 07:43.374
Kevin James, why'd you have
to come back to television?

07:43.409 --> 07:45.376
I ate Adam Sandler.

07:45.411 --> 07:47.211
Uh, yoo-hoo!

07:47.246 --> 07:49.280
I'm in here
with the pizza.

07:51.751 --> 07:53.717
Okay, time to go to Africa
and get my money back.

07:53.753 --> 07:55.119
Are you ready?

07:55.154 --> 07:57.121
I was born three
months early.

07:57.156 --> 07:58.956
Peter, who's
that at the door?

07:58.991 --> 08:00.958
Oh, just so you know, I didn't
tell Lois where we're going,

08:00.993 --> 08:02.960
and I couldn't be
touched until I was two.

08:02.995 --> 08:04.395
Daddy, what are
you doing here?!

08:04.430 --> 08:05.996
Oh, hey, Lois.

08:06.032 --> 08:07.832
Uh, Carter and I are going away
for the next week or so.

08:07.867 --> 08:09.266
You are? Where?

08:09.302 --> 08:11.669
Oh, uh... we're, uh...

08:11.704 --> 08:13.671
I mean, um...

08:13.706 --> 08:14.672
Pinterest!

08:14.707 --> 08:15.673
Wow, sounds great.

08:15.708 --> 08:16.841
Have fun.

08:16.876 --> 08:18.108
This is getting easier.

08:18.144 --> 08:20.110
Now I just say
daytime-mom words.

08:20.146 --> 08:21.512
Okay, so see you soon,

08:21.547 --> 08:23.347
<i>and... Chablis The View.</i>

08:23.382 --> 08:24.782
Aw, you too,
sweetheart.

08:24.817 --> 08:26.383
Bye.

08:30.556 --> 08:33.257
I'm telling you, you wouldn't
believe Patty's body.

08:33.292 --> 08:36.260
Just, uh, a tiny waist,
firm butt, great rack.

08:36.295 --> 08:38.095
♪ She's in high school. ♪

08:38.130 --> 08:39.930
<i>I know, and she's
in high school.</i>

08:39.966 --> 08:41.131
It's, like,
7:00 a.m., dude.

08:41.167 --> 08:42.333
Calm down.

08:42.368 --> 08:44.335
Meg, hey, how's it going?

08:44.370 --> 08:45.636
Uh, hey, Brian.

08:45.671 --> 08:46.770
Cool, that's
great to hear.

08:46.806 --> 08:47.806
Hey, where's Patty?

08:47.840 --> 08:48.806
Oh, I don't know.

08:48.841 --> 08:50.174
Probably at her house?

08:50.209 --> 08:52.009
You're
hilarious, Meg.

08:52.044 --> 08:54.445
Hey, so, uh, what kind of movies
do you and your friends like?

08:54.480 --> 08:55.846
Well, Ruth likes...
Not her.

08:55.882 --> 08:57.281
Esther likes...
Not her.

08:57.316 --> 08:58.549
I like...
Patty, just Patty.

08:58.584 --> 09:00.551
Oh, she loves anything

09:00.586 --> 09:02.987
where a teenage girl
is sick and dies of cancer.

09:03.022 --> 09:05.389
Or any movie where
a character is named Patty.

09:05.424 --> 09:07.491
Ugh, she loses
her mind for that.

09:07.527 --> 09:10.528
Well, okay, Miss Chatterbox,
you better get off to school.

09:11.931 --> 09:14.331
Wow, you're really
obsessed with Patty.

09:14.367 --> 09:16.834
You want her even more than
I wanted the new iPhone.

09:16.869 --> 09:18.469
How's it going?
Good.

09:18.504 --> 09:19.870
Just looking forward to
getting that new phone.

09:19.906 --> 09:20.871
What are you
talking about?

09:20.907 --> 09:22.306
This isn't
the Apple store.

09:22.341 --> 09:23.707
This is
a super-gay club.

09:23.743 --> 09:26.143
Yeah, right, I leave
and you get my phone.

09:26.178 --> 09:28.345
Nice try, cutie pie.

09:28.381 --> 09:30.381
♪ ♪

09:43.229 --> 09:46.196
Wow, there's so much
wildlife in Africa.

09:46.232 --> 09:48.198
You know, they say there's
some animal species here

09:48.234 --> 09:49.600
that haven't even
been discovered yet.

09:49.635 --> 09:51.035
Is that right?

09:51.070 --> 09:52.870
Yes, that is right.

09:52.905 --> 09:54.805
Oh, my God,
look over there!

09:57.310 --> 09:59.109
That African warlord
is brutalizing

09:59.145 --> 10:00.945
those innocent people.
Yeah, but it's okay,

10:00.980 --> 10:02.780
because he's wearing
a large cowboy hat

10:02.815 --> 10:04.615
and follows everything
with "hamburger,"

10:04.650 --> 10:06.617
like that stand-up
comic from the '90s.

10:06.652 --> 10:10.588
We are going to force all these
young boys to be child soldiers.

10:10.623 --> 10:12.423
Hamburger.

10:13.659 --> 10:15.459
After 18 hours in the mines,

10:15.494 --> 10:17.461
we are going to check
your butts for diamonds.

10:17.496 --> 10:19.096
Hamburger.

10:19.131 --> 10:20.397
I get it.

10:20.433 --> 10:21.398
If you do not work

10:21.434 --> 10:22.399
on my rubber plantation,

10:22.435 --> 10:24.368
I will burn your tongues.

10:24.403 --> 10:25.703
Oh, my God!

10:25.738 --> 10:27.104
Hamburger.

10:28.574 --> 10:29.540
Ah, I found him.

10:29.575 --> 10:31.542
Alonzo "Hamburger" Jones.

10:31.577 --> 10:34.445
He made it to YouTube.
Must be filthy rich.

10:38.918 --> 10:40.284
Oh, my God!

10:40.319 --> 10:42.286
I didn't expect to
see you guys here.

10:42.321 --> 10:44.722
So teenagers know
about the mall, too?

10:44.757 --> 10:46.090
Know what
about the mall?

10:46.125 --> 10:47.091
Yeah, right?

10:47.126 --> 10:49.093
Boy, the day I'm having.

10:49.128 --> 10:50.928
I actually made
one too many Build-a-Bears

10:50.963 --> 10:52.329
for the cancer kids.

10:52.365 --> 10:54.498
If only I could build
a cure, huh?

10:54.533 --> 10:56.734
Aw...
Hey, you know what, Patty?

10:56.769 --> 10:58.302
Why don't you take
the extra one?

10:58.337 --> 10:59.637
Wow, thanks, Brian.

10:59.672 --> 11:00.904
Yeah, that's cool, Brian.

11:00.940 --> 11:02.406
Will you buy me a hat at Lids?

11:02.441 --> 11:03.907
No. You know, Patty,

11:03.943 --> 11:06.143
I've got $7.50 left
on my Panda Express card

11:06.178 --> 11:07.845
if you want to split
a three-item combo.

11:07.880 --> 11:09.246
No drink.
Sure!

11:09.281 --> 11:12.016
Well, then, hop on board
the Panda Express!

11:12.051 --> 11:14.118
In bed, right?

11:14.153 --> 11:16.520
Like-like with the fortune
cookies, you know...

11:16.555 --> 11:18.822
Brian, can I talk
to you for a second?

11:18.858 --> 11:20.658
What the hell
is going on?

11:20.693 --> 11:22.359
You're hitting on Patty
and it's gross.

11:22.395 --> 11:23.627
She's 18!

11:23.663 --> 11:25.462
Stop it!
Me?

11:25.498 --> 11:27.264
Meg, I am not even
going to dignify that

11:27.299 --> 11:28.866
with a mall erection.

11:28.901 --> 11:31.101
Don't...
don't look down.

11:36.709 --> 11:38.809
Well, we made it.

11:38.844 --> 11:40.711
East Bola.

11:40.746 --> 11:44.882
All right, let's find our
"prince" and get my money back.

11:44.917 --> 11:46.150
Get down!

11:46.185 --> 11:47.551
On the ground!

11:47.586 --> 11:48.819
This is unacceptable.

11:48.854 --> 11:50.688
I demand to speak
to Anthony Anderson.

11:55.594 --> 11:57.394
Okay, hold on.
Shoot me if you must,

11:57.430 --> 11:59.663
but it is imperative
that I answer this call.

12:01.801 --> 12:03.300
Yello?

12:03.335 --> 12:04.868
Yes, this is Peter Griffin.

12:04.904 --> 12:08.205
Yes, I did call you about the
eight-piece lawn croquet set.

12:08.240 --> 12:11.008
Now, it says "weathered,"
just how weathered is it?

12:11.043 --> 12:14.011
Yeah, go ahead and send me
a pic, that'd be very helpful.

12:15.281 --> 12:16.880
Sir, shoot me if you must,

12:16.916 --> 12:19.483
but it is imperative
that I look at these pictures.

12:25.853 --> 12:27.085
The hell with this.

12:27.121 --> 12:28.220
I'm getting my money back

12:28.255 --> 12:29.655
if it's the last
thing I do.

12:29.690 --> 12:31.557
Hey, here's the guys.

12:31.592 --> 12:33.592
Who are you
and why are you here?

12:33.627 --> 12:35.060
I'm Carter Pewterschmidt,

12:35.095 --> 12:36.862
and I'm here because
you stole my money!

12:36.897 --> 12:39.198
You?
You are Carter Pewterschmidt?

12:39.233 --> 12:40.499
You're damn right I am!

12:40.534 --> 12:41.867
Oh! It's him!

12:41.902 --> 12:44.069
It's the Great Father
Pewterschmidt!

12:44.104 --> 12:46.438
What's happening?
What's he talking about?

12:46.473 --> 12:48.507
You are a great hero to us.

12:48.542 --> 12:50.242
It is with the money
that you sent

12:50.277 --> 12:51.877
that we have been able to make

12:51.912 --> 12:53.946
many wonderful improvements
to our village.

12:53.981 --> 12:56.114
And he used my computer.

12:56.150 --> 12:58.450
I'm Griff, by the way,
that's what everybody calls me.

12:58.485 --> 13:00.619
That's not true.
Nobody calls him that.

13:03.390 --> 13:05.958
It was your money that
paid for the school,

13:05.993 --> 13:08.594
a well to provide
clean drinking water,

13:08.629 --> 13:10.796
our first health clinic,

13:10.831 --> 13:13.398
and a Redbox with
one movie in it.

13:13.434 --> 13:14.867
<i>It's Baby Geniuses.</i>

13:14.902 --> 13:16.835
Which I, personally,
could begin watching

13:16.871 --> 13:18.904
at any point in the film
and enjoy from there.

13:18.939 --> 13:20.772
Oh, yeah, that's how
I feel about that video

13:20.808 --> 13:22.474
of Kelsey Grammer
fallin' off the stage.

13:22.509 --> 13:23.809
I don't understand.

13:23.844 --> 13:25.577
So there never was
a Nigerian prince?

13:25.613 --> 13:29.381
No. You see, no one will
actually give money to Africa

13:29.416 --> 13:30.949
unless they are tricked into it.

13:30.985 --> 13:32.718
So again, we thank you

13:32.753 --> 13:34.620
for your generosity,
Father Pewterschmidt.

13:34.655 --> 13:36.121
Well, I hope you enjoyed it...

13:36.156 --> 13:37.389
'cause I'm taking it all back.

13:37.424 --> 13:38.156
What?
What?

13:38.192 --> 13:39.324
You heard me!

13:39.360 --> 13:40.592
Nobody steals
from Carter Pewterschmidt

13:40.628 --> 13:41.827
and gets away with it!

13:41.862 --> 13:43.395
Carter, why you
bein' so mean?

13:43.430 --> 13:44.630
The money's spent.

13:44.665 --> 13:46.632
And look how happy
you made these people.

13:46.667 --> 13:48.734
Talk to me--
it's your buddy Griff.

13:48.769 --> 13:50.335
Tear it all down! Now.

13:50.371 --> 13:52.304
Or I'm canceling Kwanzaa.

13:52.339 --> 13:53.572
What is Kwanzaa?

13:53.607 --> 13:55.507
Ah!
I knew it wasn't real!

13:59.213 --> 14:00.612
Hey, there, babe.

14:00.648 --> 14:01.847
Hey, Brian.

14:01.882 --> 14:03.282
You ready?

14:03.317 --> 14:05.150
Got the Smash Mouth
cued up in the Pri.

14:05.185 --> 14:06.425
Brian, what are you doing here?

14:06.453 --> 14:08.320
I'm here to
pick up Patty.

14:08.355 --> 14:10.355
<i>We're going to see a movie
called Brittany Finds a Lump.</i>

14:10.391 --> 14:12.357
You're parked in
Mr. Tackleman's space.

14:12.393 --> 14:13.959
You're going on a date
with Patty?

14:13.994 --> 14:15.427
I told you to back off.

14:15.462 --> 14:17.429
And since when
do you wear high-tops?

14:17.464 --> 14:18.430
What, my kicks?

14:18.465 --> 14:19.665
Ah, it's nothin'.

14:19.700 --> 14:21.099
I just use these
for Instagram.

14:21.135 --> 14:22.334
That's something I like!

14:22.369 --> 14:23.602
Ah, shut up, Esther!

14:23.637 --> 14:25.337
All right, we're out of here.

14:25.372 --> 14:27.806
Feel free to use the seat
warmer, keep that box hot.

14:29.310 --> 14:31.476
♪ Somebody once told me ♪

14:31.512 --> 14:33.378
♪ The world is gonna... ♪

14:40.888 --> 14:43.155
Geez, I can't believe you're
going through with this, Carter.

14:43.190 --> 14:45.157
Paying these thugs
to tear down the village

14:45.192 --> 14:46.391
isn't gonna bring
your money back.

14:46.427 --> 14:48.026
This isn't about the money.

14:48.062 --> 14:50.395
This is payback for Sammy
Davis dating Kim Novak.

14:50.431 --> 14:52.431
Oh, come on, Carter,
don't do this.

14:52.466 --> 14:54.399
You don't want to be
the first white guy

14:54.435 --> 14:55.634
to do something
bad to Africa.

14:55.669 --> 14:56.969
Are you about done?

14:57.004 --> 14:58.203
I'm supposed to go
lion shooting

14:58.238 --> 14:59.805
with a scumbag dentist.

15:03.610 --> 15:06.345
Oh, my God, they're even taking
down the mosquito netting.

15:09.216 --> 15:12.050
♪ Buzz, buzz, buzz. ♪

15:13.687 --> 15:15.487
No, Carter, I can't
let you do this!

15:15.522 --> 15:16.922
I won't stand by

15:16.957 --> 15:18.757
and let you further ruin
this terrible place!

15:18.792 --> 15:20.325
Oh, is that right?

15:20.361 --> 15:22.060
Yes, that is right.

15:22.096 --> 15:23.762
Here's 5,000 bucks.

15:23.797 --> 15:25.063
Lock up that fat-ass.

15:30.604 --> 15:33.071
Damn it, this sucks.

15:33.107 --> 15:34.773
I may never get out of here.

15:34.808 --> 15:37.843
Well, as a man
falsely imprisoned in Africa,

15:37.878 --> 15:40.579
I have no choice but to write
a memoir of my struggles.

15:40.614 --> 15:42.881
"Chapter One:

15:42.916 --> 15:46.284
"Harry Potter's aunt and uncle
were super mean.

15:46.320 --> 15:49.721
"'Spank me harder,' the lady
says to Fifty Shades of Grey.

15:49.757 --> 15:52.257
"'That's Mr. Fifty
Shades of Grey

15:52.292 --> 15:54.059
<i>"to you,
Kate from Ben and Kate.'</i>

15:54.094 --> 15:56.228
"And then he turned her butt
inside out.

15:56.263 --> 15:58.196
Because, sexy."

15:58.232 --> 16:00.932
"'Isn't that special,'
said the Church Lady,

16:00.968 --> 16:03.235
"before reporting
for her botched surgery.

16:03.270 --> 16:05.604
"Anyway, I'm here in a prison
against my will,

16:05.639 --> 16:06.872
"and I should be free.

16:06.907 --> 16:09.374
The end."

16:09.410 --> 16:10.942
Take this, Cheebo.

16:10.978 --> 16:13.045
Take this to a French-Canadian
flight attendant.

16:13.080 --> 16:15.247
And he will give it
to everybody.

16:26.527 --> 16:27.893
Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker.

16:27.928 --> 16:30.462
Our top story:
sinking newscaster.

16:31.665 --> 16:33.398
Just kidding, it's the chair.

16:33.434 --> 16:36.501
But, in other news, domestic
abuse enthusiast Paul Simon

16:36.537 --> 16:39.104
has released a new song
inspired by a memoir

16:39.139 --> 16:41.440
written by Quahog's
own Peter Griffin,

16:41.475 --> 16:43.842
who has been falsely imprisoned
by his father-in-law

16:43.877 --> 16:45.310
in an African jail.

16:45.345 --> 16:47.446
Oh, for God's sake.

16:47.481 --> 16:50.449
I bet there's not one word
about you in that book.

16:54.354 --> 16:56.254
Wow, what a beautiful night.

16:56.290 --> 16:58.090
Yeah.

16:58.125 --> 17:00.592
Hey, I wonder if any of those
stars are wishing on us, huh?

17:00.627 --> 17:02.594
You're so deep.

17:02.629 --> 17:04.529
I betcha you're
pretty deep, too.

17:04.565 --> 17:07.432
Aw, you're so sweet.

17:07.468 --> 17:09.434
Why are you so nice to me?

17:09.470 --> 17:11.169
Most guys never give me
the time of day

17:11.205 --> 17:12.804
because I'm so plain-looking.

17:12.840 --> 17:14.473
Well, I'm not
like most guys.

17:14.508 --> 17:15.974
I can see past
that sweater.

17:16.009 --> 17:17.442
Speaking of which,

17:17.478 --> 17:19.158
why don't we get rid
of that big old thing?

17:20.314 --> 17:21.513
Brian, stop!

17:21.548 --> 17:23.215
You don't have
to do this, Patty.

17:23.250 --> 17:24.950
Brian's just taking
advantage of you.

17:24.985 --> 17:26.451
What? That's crazy!

17:26.487 --> 17:28.553
What?
Why would he do that?

17:28.589 --> 17:30.522
Because you have
an amazing body.

17:30.557 --> 17:31.790
I do?

17:31.825 --> 17:33.291
But... you're always saying

17:33.327 --> 17:35.794
dumpy girls like us
only have each other.

17:35.829 --> 17:37.362
You're not dumpy.

17:37.397 --> 17:38.897
I was just saying that

17:38.932 --> 17:40.298
because I was worried
you'd become popular

17:40.334 --> 17:42.000
and not want to be friends
with us anymore.

17:42.035 --> 17:43.835
Meg, I'm $18
into this evening,

17:43.871 --> 17:45.470
so can you maybe
just get out of here?

17:45.506 --> 17:46.872
Meg, that's silly.

17:46.907 --> 17:48.740
I'll always be your friend.

17:48.775 --> 17:50.342
You promise?

17:50.377 --> 17:52.677
♪ ♪

17:56.950 --> 17:59.384
Oh, come on, what the hell?

17:59.419 --> 18:00.652
Bummer.

18:00.687 --> 18:02.187
He's never gonna
get to hit that.

18:02.222 --> 18:04.156
I know. That's exactly
what I wished for.

18:04.191 --> 18:07.726
Well, I actually wished
for it 30,000 years ago.

18:07.761 --> 18:09.761
♪ ♪

18:12.432 --> 18:13.765
It's true.

18:13.800 --> 18:15.367
Even at the speed of light,

18:15.402 --> 18:17.536
mean-spirited thoughts
from the stars

18:17.571 --> 18:19.938
can take thousands or
even millions of years

18:19.973 --> 18:22.507
to reach the Earth.

18:22.543 --> 18:24.943
Ham-burger.

18:30.551 --> 18:32.918
♪ There's a great man
locked up in a cell ♪

18:32.953 --> 18:35.420
♪ The African folks
all know him well ♪

18:35.455 --> 18:37.856
♪ He's a great spirit
with a lot to say ♪

18:37.891 --> 18:40.425
♪ That's why they locked
Peter Griffin away ♪

18:40.460 --> 18:43.061
♪ There's a breeze
that's in the air ♪

18:43.096 --> 18:45.797
♪ Peter Griffin in my hair ♪

18:45.832 --> 18:48.099
♪ Peter Griffin up my nose ♪

18:48.135 --> 18:50.769
♪ In my lungs
and down to my toes ♪

18:50.804 --> 18:53.271
♪ Peter Griffin in my skin ♪

18:53.307 --> 18:55.473
♪ Everybody breathe him in ♪

18:55.509 --> 18:58.076
♪ Peter Griffin ♪

18:58.111 --> 19:00.478
♪ Freedom for Peter Griffin ♪

19:00.514 --> 19:02.981
♪ Peter Griffin ♪

19:03.016 --> 19:06.117
♪ Let my Peter go. ♪

19:06.153 --> 19:07.586
Now wait, let me
get this straight:

19:07.621 --> 19:09.888
none of you guys has
ever heard of Bono?

19:09.923 --> 19:11.122
He says he knows you.

19:11.158 --> 19:12.991
Daddy! What the hell
are you doing?

19:13.026 --> 19:14.593
You threw Peter in jail?

19:14.628 --> 19:16.728
Hey, Pumpkin, welcome!

19:16.763 --> 19:18.830
Whatever you do, don't tell
them you have a clitoris.

19:18.865 --> 19:20.665
Yeah, they told me
that at the embassy.

19:20.701 --> 19:22.500
Look, I'm sorry
you got swindled,

19:22.536 --> 19:24.669
but you can't treat
people this way.

19:24.705 --> 19:27.005
You let Peter out of
that jail right now.

19:27.040 --> 19:28.340
And give these
people back

19:28.375 --> 19:29.815
their health clinic
and their school.

19:29.843 --> 19:31.076
No.

19:31.111 --> 19:33.078
Hi, Lois!
I like your shorts!

19:33.113 --> 19:34.479
Bye, Lois!

19:34.514 --> 19:35.780
Oh, my God!

19:35.816 --> 19:37.015
Enough is enough!

19:37.050 --> 19:38.283
That's your son-in-law!

19:38.318 --> 19:39.484
And my husband!

19:39.519 --> 19:42.053
I know how
families work, Lois.

19:42.089 --> 19:44.089
All right.
Let him go.

19:44.124 --> 19:46.124
Yay!

19:46.159 --> 19:47.392
Lois, how much was your flight

19:47.427 --> 19:48.793
and which card
did you put it on?

19:48.829 --> 19:50.996
Daddy, I don't
understand any of this.

19:51.031 --> 19:52.897
I mean, you've
always been grouchy,

19:52.933 --> 19:55.433
but why are you being
so mean-spirited?

19:55.469 --> 19:57.168
What's gotten into you?

19:57.204 --> 19:59.604
What's gotten into me?
I'm angry!

19:59.640 --> 20:01.206
For God's sake, I can't
even be left alone

20:01.241 --> 20:02.841
in my own house
for an afternoon.

20:02.876 --> 20:04.643
You have to drop me
off at your house

20:04.678 --> 20:06.711
so this fat idiot
can babysit me!

20:06.747 --> 20:08.546
I'm old and it sucks!

20:08.582 --> 20:10.448
I'm sorry, Daddy.

20:10.484 --> 20:12.617
I realize growing old is no fun,

20:12.653 --> 20:14.686
but this is no way to act.

20:14.721 --> 20:16.054
I know.

20:16.089 --> 20:18.123
I'm sorry I almost had you shot.

20:18.158 --> 20:19.357
Oh, that's all right.

20:19.393 --> 20:20.892
I got a fever
of a 108.

20:20.927 --> 20:22.627
I'm not gonna
remember any of this.

20:22.663 --> 20:25.030
And I'm sorry for what
I did to your village, Dave.

20:25.065 --> 20:26.298
His name is "Dave"?

20:26.333 --> 20:28.700
Yeah. Get to know
these people, okay?

20:28.735 --> 20:30.835
Listen, when I get home,
I'll transfer enough money

20:30.871 --> 20:32.470
so you can rebuild your town.

20:32.506 --> 20:34.172
You've all been very kind.

20:34.207 --> 20:35.573
Yeah, this has been great, guys.

20:35.609 --> 20:37.309
Now all I need is a group photo

20:37.344 --> 20:39.010
of me kneeling
in the front of the village,

20:39.046 --> 20:41.112
so I can brag about
what a good person I am.

20:51.782 --> 20:58.282
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru